    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb9afa65a8aaa4f838d9333ccf47e4216b284"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/RenalCyst"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb9afa65a8aaa4f838d9333ccf47e4216b285"/>
    <skos:definition>A renal cyst whose contents are not uniformly fluid.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>complex renal cyst</skos:prefLabel>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:created>
    <cde:designNote>Carries calcification; the parent does not. A simple cyst does not calcify, and a calcified renal cyst is Bosniak II or above, which is complex by definition.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:designNote>Defined class: conditions are necessary and sufficient, so a reasoner classifies into it. Nothing about it is authored twice.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:lastModified>
